From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:12:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] linux-dmabuf: hide AFBC modifiers the display cannot scan out

Rockchip VOP/VOP2 and Amlogic OSD planes reject AFBC TILED and SC
layouts. When advertised, libmali picks them and the buffer can only
be composited.
---
 types/wlr_linux_dmabuf_v1.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/types/wlr_linux_dmabuf_v1.c b/types/wlr_linux_dmabuf_v1.c
index b885c25..ea75df9 100644
--- a/types/wlr_linux_dmabuf_v1.c
+++ b/types/wlr_linux_dmabuf_v1.c
@@ -811,6 +811,12 @@ static void linux_dmabuf_send_modifiers(struct wl_resource *resource,
 
 	for (size_t i = 0; i < fmt->len; i++) {
 		uint64_t mod = fmt->modifiers[i];
+		// Rockchip VOP/VOP2 and Amlogic OSD cannot scan out TILED or SC AFBC
+		if (mod >> 56 == DRM_FORMAT_MOD_VENDOR_ARM &&
+				((mod >> 52) & 0xf) == DRM_FORMAT_MOD_ARM_TYPE_AFBC &&
+				(mod & (AFBC_FORMAT_MOD_TILED | AFBC_FORMAT_MOD_SC))) {
+			continue;
+		}
 		zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1_send_modifier(resource, fmt->format,
 			mod >> 32, mod & 0xFFFFFFFF);
 	}
